nsion variance across all 20 latent dimensions.\n3. What happens to the latent dimensions under $\\beta = 10.0$? Provide a explanation why does a large $\\beta$ incentivize the encoder to ignore the input? Why does the decoder then receive no useful signal from those dimensions?","metadata":{"id":"q32-header"}},{"id":"active-dims","cell_type":"code","source":"def compute_active_dims(model, loader, device=DEVICE):\n    model.eval()\n    all_mu = []\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for x, _ in loader:\n            mu, _ = model.encoder(x.to(device))\n            all_mu.append(mu.cpu())\n    all_mu = torch.cat(all_mu, dim=0)   \n    return all_mu.var(dim=0)            \n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 4), sharey=False)\nz_dim = Z_DIM\n\nfor ax, beta in zip(axes, betas):\n    m   = histories[beta][\"model\"]\n    var = compute_active_dims(m, test_loader)\n    ax.bar(range(z_dim), var.numpy(), color=colors[beta], alpha=0.8)\n    ax.axhline(y=0.01, color='black', linestyle='--', linewidth=1,\n               label='Collapse threshold (0.01)')\n    ax.set_title(f'β = {beta}')\n    ax.set_xlabel('Latent Dimension')\n    ax.set_ylabel('Var of μ across test set')\n    ax.legend(fontsize=8)\n\nplt.suptitle('Per-Dimension Variance of Encoder Means (Active Dimensions)')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('active_dims.png', dpi=150)\nplt.show()","metadata":{"id":"active-dims","trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-02T16:59:52.187883Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-02T16:59:52.188266Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.118171Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-05-02T16:59:52.18822Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.117343Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1600x400 with 3 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":11},{"id":"part4-header","cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## Part 4  Geometry of the Latent Space\n\n### Q4.1  Linear Interpolation (15 pts)\n\nA well-trained VAE should produce a smooth, connected latent space: nearby points in $\\mathbb{R}^d$ should decode to semantically similar images.\n\nUsing your $\\beta = 1.0$ model:\n\n1. Pick one test image of digit \"2\" and one of digit \"7\". Pass each through the encoder and record the **mean vectors** $\\mu_A$ and $\\mu_B$ (use the mean, not a sample).\n2. Generate 10 interpolated latent vectors: $z_t = (1-t)\\,\\mu_A + t\\,\\mu_B,\\quad t \\in \\{0.0,\\,0.1,\\,\\ldots,\\,1.0\\}$\n3. Decode each $z_t$ and display the resulting images.\n4. Do you observe a smooth semantic transition? Describe what the intermediate images look like. Why does the KL regularization term play a direct role in enabling this, while a standard Autoencoder (no KL term) would not guarantee it?","metadata":{"id":"part4-header"}},{"id":"interpolation","cell_type":"code","source":"model_beta1 = histories[1.0][\"model\"]\nmodel_beta1.eval()\n\nimg_A = img_B = None\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    for x, y in test_loader:\n        for i in range(len(y)):\n            if img_A is None and y[i].item() == 2:\n                img_A = x[i].to(DEVICE)\n            if img_B is None and y[i].item() == 7:\n                img_B = x[i].to(DEVICE)\n            if img_A is not None and img_B is not None:\n                break\n        if img_A is not None and img_B is not None:\n            break\n\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    mu_A, _ = model_beta1.encoder(img_A.unsqueeze(0))\n    mu_B, _ = model_beta1.encoder(img_B.unsqueeze(0))\n\nts = torch.linspace(0, 1, 10)\ninterp_images = []\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    for t in ts:\n        z_t   = (1 - t) * mu_A + t * mu_B\n        img_t = model_beta1.decoder(z_t)\n        interp_images.append(img_t.cpu().squeeze())\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 10, figsize=(18, 2))\nfor i, ax in enumerate(axes):\n    ax.imshow(interp_images[i].numpy(), cmap='gray', vmin=0, vmax=1)\n    ax.set_title(f't={ts[i]:.1f}', fontsize=8)\n    ax.axis('off')\n\naxes[0].set_title('t=0.0\\n(digit 2)', fontsize=8)\naxes[-1].set_title('t=1.0\\n(digit 7)', fontsize=8)\n\nplt.suptitle('Latent Space Linear Interpolation: \"2\" → \"7\"  (β=1.0)', y=1.05)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('interpolation.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()","metadata":{"id":"interpolation","trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.119137Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.119482Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.786874Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.119441Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.786047Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1800x200 with 10 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":12},{"id":"q42-header","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Q4.2 — 2-D Latent Space Visualization *(Bonus, 10 pts)*\n\nRetrain a VAE with `Z_DIM = 2`. Encode the full test set, collect all $\\mu$ vectors, and plot them colored by digit class. Describe the structure: are digit classes separated? Do visually similar digits cluster near each other?","metadata":{"id":"q42-header"}},{"id":"latent-viz","cell_type":"code","source":"Z_DIM_2D = 2\nmodel_2d  = VAE(z_dim=Z_DIM_2D).to(DEVICE)\nopt_2d    = optim.Adam(model_2d.parameters(), lr=LR)\nprint(\"Training 2-D VAE...\")\ntrain(model_2d, opt_2d, vae_loss, train_loader)\n\nmodel_2d.eval()\nall_mu     = []\nall_labels = []\n\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    for x, y in test_loader:\n        mu, _ = model_2d.encoder(x.to(DEVICE))\n        all_mu.append(mu.cpu())\n        all_labels.append(y)\n\n\nall_mu     = torch.cat(all_mu,     dim=0).numpy()\nall_labels = torch.cat(all_labels, dim=0).numpy()\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 9))\ncmap    = plt.cm.get_cmap('tab10', 10)\n\nfor digit in range(10):\n    mask = all_labels == digit\n    ax.scatter(all_mu[mask, 0], all_mu[mask, 1],\n               s=4, alpha=0.35, color=cmap(digit), label=str(digit))\n    cx, cy = all_mu[mask, 0].mean(), all_mu[mask, 1].mean()\n    ax.annotate(str(digit), xy=(cx, cy), fontsize=15, fontweight='bold',\n                color='white',\n                bbox=dict(boxstyle='round,pad=0.3', facecolor=cmap(digit),\n                          edgecolor='black', linewidth=0.8, alpha=0.9),\n                ha='center', va='center', zorder=5)\n\nax.set_title('2-D VAE Latent Space — Test Set μ Vectors Colored by Digit Class',\n             fontsize=13, pad=12)\nax.set_xlabel('z₁', fontsize=12)\nax.set_ylabel('z₂', fontsize=12)\nax.legend(title='Digit', markerscale=6, loc='upper right',\n          fontsize=9, framealpha=0.8)\nax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.3)\n\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('latent_2d_labeled.png', dpi=150)\nplt.show()","metadata":{"id":"latent-viz","trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.788081Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.788738Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-02T17:02:18.261149Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-05-02T16:59:56.78871Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-02T17:02:18.260362Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Training 2-D VAE...\nEpoch 01/20 | Recon: 46.3304 | KL: 2.1512 | Total: 48.4816\nEpoch 02/20 | Recon: 36.8839 | KL: 3.7118 | Total: 40.5957\nEpoch 03/20 | Recon: 34.6756 | KL: 4.1599 | Total: 38.8355\nEpoch 04/20 | Recon: 33.5657 | KL: 4.3788 | Total: 37.9445\nEpoch 05/20 | Recon: 32.8290 | KL: 4.5239 | Total: 37.3529\nEpoch 06/20 | Recon: 32.2725 | KL: 4.6301 | Total: 36.9027\nEpoch 07/20 | Recon: 31.8326 | KL: 4.7231 | Total: 36.5557\nEpoch 08/20 | Recon: 31.4846 | KL: 4.8015 | Total: 36.2861\nEpoch 09/20 | Recon: 31.1681 | KL: 4.8667 | Total: 36.0349\nEpoch 10/20 | Recon: 30.9042 | KL: 4.9102 | Total: 35.8144\nEpoch 11/20 | Recon: 30.6409 | KL: 4.9773 | Total: 35.6182\nEpoch 12/20 | Recon: 30.4339 | KL: 5.0308 | Total: 35.4648\nEpoch 13/20 | Recon: 30.2130 | KL: 5.0655 | Total: 35.2784\nEpoch 14/20 | Recon: 30.0490 | KL: 5.1093 | Total: 35.1583\nEpoch 15/20 | Recon: 29.8775 | KL: 5.1436 | Total: 35.0212\nEpoc